 "summary": "The post-PR surface is minimal and characteristically complete: `mellinDis_def`/`mellinDisConvergent_def` use `(rfl)`/`(Iff.rfl)` so no defeq leaks, both Mathlib bridges transport values and convergence (indicator and support forms), and the general indicator/power-weight lemmas are public in HalfLine.lean under the root namespaces. The three `private` helpers are one-line specialisations of that public API, the `@[expose]` in Strip.lean exposes no body (the file has no `def`), and the sole `@[simp]` lemma has a closed head and cannot loop.",
